# Lullabeast environment (install.sh writes .env on first install; copy this file as a template).
# Source before running:  source .env
#
# Canonical variable names (legacy alias AUTODEV_ROOT and the removed
# AUTODEV_USE_LEGACY_OPENCLAW_RUNTIME have no effect):
#   OPENCLAW_ROOT         — OpenClaw installation root
#   AUTODEV_PIPELINE_ROOT — pipeline state directory (defaults under the repo)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Core (required)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OpenClaw installation root: contains workspaces, openclaw.json, and the
# pipeline-project symlink target. Default is ~/.openclaw. For Docker or a
# bind-mounted data dir, set this to the host path that holds workspace-planner,
# openclaw.json, etc. Must match ui/config.json `openclaw_root`.
OPENCLAW_ROOT=~/.openclaw

# This repository root (contains autodev/pipeline/orchestrator.py).
AUTODEV_REPO_PATH=/path/to/autodev-ui

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pipeline state (optional — defaults to $AUTODEV_REPO_PATH/.autodev)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Directory that holds pipeline.lock, pipeline_state.json, pipeline_queue.json,
# orchestrator.log, and the pipeline-project symlink. The repo-local default
# (<repo>/.autodev) is correct for most installs. Set this to the OpenClaw root
# if you want pipeline state to live alongside OpenClaw data (e.g. Docker
# bind-mounts where the orchestrator and agents must share a single tree).
# AUTODEV_PIPELINE_ROOT=/absolute/path/here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Webhook (required for UI → OpenClaw agent launches)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bearer token used by the UI when POSTing to /hooks/agent. Overrides
# `hooks_token` in ui/config.json when set. Install.sh copies the value from
# openclaw.json → hooks.token so the three sources stay in sync.
# AUTODEV_HOOKS_TOKEN=your-hooks-token-from-openclaw.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard access token (UI auth)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Required by the UI server for the dashboard and /api/*: authorize a browser
# once via the startup URL (http://127.0.0.1:18790/?token=...), or send
# 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' from scripts. Overrides `ui_token` in
# ui/config.json when set. install.sh generates a random value here. Unset =
# legacy open mode: loopback is served unauthenticated and non-loopback
# requests are refused.
# AUTODEV_UI_TOKEN=your-dashboard-access-token

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Audit (optional)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Phase audit snapshots: absolute path or ~. Unset → $OPENCLAW_ROOT/pipeline-audit.
# Set to empty string to disable snapshots entirely.
# AUTODEV_AUDIT_ARCHIVE_DIR=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tier A stall timeouts (optional — orchestrator only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- AutoDev: Tier A stall timeouts (optional) ---
# Two-knob stall detection (autodev/pipeline/sentinel_poller.py:poll_for_sentinel).
# STARTUP_GRACE bounds the pre-first-hook wait; STALL_TIMEOUT bounds the
# post-first-hook silence. They are independent — tune cold OpenClaw boot time
# with STARTUP_GRACE and mid-turn-silence detection with STALL_TIMEOUT.
# Uncomment a line and set an integer to override the built-in default.
# Built-in defaults if unset:
#   STALL_TIMEOUT_*  (post-first-hook silence) — planner/executor/reviewer = 300 s
#   STARTUP_GRACE_*  (pre-first-hook wait)      — planner/executor/reviewer = 600 s
# AUTODEV_STALL_TIMEOUT_PLANNER=
# AUTODEV_STALL_TIMEOUT_EXECUTOR=
# AUTODEV_STALL_TIMEOUT_REVIEWER=
# AUTODEV_STARTUP_GRACE_PLANNER=
# AUTODEV_STARTUP_GRACE_EXECUTOR=
# AUTODEV_STARTUP_GRACE_REVIEWER=

# --- AutoDev: Tool-loop catcher sensitivity (optional) ---
# Per-role threshold (count) of CONSECUTIVE identical tool calls — same tool, same
# input, nothing different between them — at which the orchestrator treats an agent
# as stuck in an in-turn loop: it stops the looping session and routes it through
# that agent's normal self-failure retry (a fresh session usually breaks the loop),
# escalating with ERR_TOOL_LOOP only if it keeps looping. Legitimately-repeated poll
# tools are excluded. Defaults if unset: planner/reviewer = 8, executor = 15 (more
# headroom for its varied tool use). Set a role to 0 to DISABLE its detector.
# TOOL_LOOP_REPEAT_LIMIT_PLANNER=
# TOOL_LOOP_REPEAT_LIMIT_EXECUTOR=
# TOOL_LOOP_REPEAT_LIMIT_REVIEWER=

# --- AutoDev: Context-overflow hold budget (optional) ---
# Layer 2 overflow-aware sentinel hold (autodev/pipeline/orchestrator.py). When an
# agent turn dies on a context-overflow error, OpenClaw auto-compacts and resumes
# the same session; the orchestrator HOLDS the premature ".done" sentinel — rather
# than escalating and discarding the verdict the resumed turn writes moments later —
# for up to this many seconds before giving up and letting the gate adjudicate.
# Bounded independently of the 75-min infrastructure backstop. Most installs never
# need to change this. Default if unset: 900.
# AUTODEV_OVERFLOW_HOLD_BUDGET=

# --- AutoDev: Provider-error retry (optional) ---
# Integer COUNT (not a 1/0 toggle): the maximum number of times a *transient*
# inference-provider rejection — an HTTP 429 / rate-limit the provider clears on
# its own — is retried before the phase escalates for human input. Each retry
# re-invokes the same agent on a fresh session and does NOT consume that agent's
# own self-failure retry budget; terminal rejections (401/402, invalid API key,
# insufficient credits) always escalate immediately because retrying cannot fix
# them. Default if unset: 0 (disabled — a provider rejection escalates on the
# first failure). Set a small positive integer (e.g. 3) for a provider that
# returns sporadic, recoverable rate-limits.
# PROVIDER_ERROR_RETRY=

# --- AutoDev: Ideas UI poll threshold (optional) ---
# UI server Ideas chat: seconds of stamp silence (after first activity) before the
# chat turn is declared a definitive stall. Env override wins over ui/config.json.
# Default if unset: 300. (No startup-grace knob — the chat send waits for a
# definitive stall/backstop verdict rather than fast-failing a slow first hook.)
# AUTODEV_IDEAS_IDLE_THRESHOLD=

# --- AutoDev: Ideas chat history budget (optional) ---
# UI server Ideas chat: hard cap on characters in the inline [CONVERSATION HISTORY]
# block prepended to each prd-creator webhook. The most recent 3 (user, assistant)
# pairs are kept inline; once that block exceeds this budget the oldest pair is
# dropped, and if a single remaining pair still exceeds the budget its content is
# truncated with a [...truncated...] marker. Older context stays available via
# ~/.openclaw/ideas/{id}/conversation_log.md, which the agent can Read on demand.
# Default if unset: 20000.
# AUTODEV_IDEAS_HISTORY_CHAR_BUDGET=
